# Day 06 — lab/terraform/.gitignore
#
# Same hygiene as Day 05, with one Day 06 addition at the bottom that matters
# more here than anywhere else in this repo.

# STATE. Plaintext JSON listing every resource this stack has touched.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Provider cache. Hundreds of MB, machine-specific, regenerated by init.
.terraform/

# Saved plans can contain sensitive values in the clear.
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Real variable values. The .example file IS the documentation and IS committed.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Lambda zips built by the archive provider at plan time.
build/
*.zip

# ==========================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: .terraform.lock.hcl
# ==========================================================================
# Commit it. It is what makes `terraform init` produce the same provider
# binary on your laptop, your colleague's laptop and in CI. Day 05's IAC-012
# is the check that catches a repo which ignores it.

# ==========================================================================
# DAY 06 ADDITION: LOG SAMPLES AND MODEL OUTPUT
# ==========================================================================
#
# During this lab you will pull windows of real CloudWatch log data down to
# your laptop to look at them before the model does, and you will save model
# responses to compare runs. Both are the highest-risk files in this repo.
#
# A CloudWatch log line from a real system contains, routinely and without
# anyone intending it: bearer tokens, session cookies, connection strings,
# email addresses, full request bodies, and stack traces with local variables
# still in them. That is exactly the same reason OBS-011 exists — the check
# that fires when a prompt template interpolates raw log text.
#
# Anything you would not paste into a public issue tracker does not belong in
# git either. These patterns are the backstop, not the policy.
logs/
log-samples/
*.log
*.logs.json
incident-*.json
summary-*.json
summary-*.txt
prompt-*.txt
